WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Hi guys, my name is Gage and I've been posting a little bit here on Substack and I wanted to

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:14.160
post a video because I wanted you to see that there was a human behind these words because I

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.760
know that a lot of the conversation about AI can feel very unhuman and can feel very

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:27.560
disjointed. So I am here today to be a human with you. And I

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:35.100
want to share a project that I have launched on myself. I call

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:45.860
it the cold mirror project. And what it is, is I bought a

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:52.460
recorder that I keep with me all the time and I run it in my

00:00:52.460 --> 00:01:01.620
household pretty often. And I do that to capture the reality

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.900
of life in my household. And the reason why I wanted to do

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:12.700
that is because I claim to be a particular type of father

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:21.020
and to be a particular type of man and even if I'm not claiming it it's what I

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:28.260
want to believe and so it's what I present but I know that what I want and

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:36.300
what I do are not always the same thing and so I wanted to test this and

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:43.260
so the way that I did this was I got the recorder and I created a project folder

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:55.800
in Claude and I created an agent a very particular set of instructions the the

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:03.480
message to the mirror was don't flatter me was help me see my blind spots

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:14.840
helped me understand if I'm actually walking the walk that I am claiming. And

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:23.140
I'm really glad that I did this. One of the important things that I needed to

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:30.300
make sure that I did for myself was that I didn't try to edit, right? There

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:40.840
are ugly moments on this. Moments that I said and did things to members of my

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:48.600
family that I am incredibly ashamed of. And it would be very easy for me to

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:56.280
not submit those entries but that would not that would defeat the

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.320
purpose completely, right? And that's not what we're here to do. That's not what I'm

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:08.160
here to do. I've learned a lot about myself during this time. I learned about my completion

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:16.880
pursuits with my kids and my Socratic extraction methods with them. And being able to compare

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:23.240
and contrast and to take in these lessons that, you know, my agent gives me, I have

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:33.410
been able to catch myself a lot faster. I have been able to repair things a lot quicker

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:41.450
and a lot cleaner. I have learned not only about myself, but I've learned more about

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:49.430
my kids and my wife. And I really think that I have become a better man and a better

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:56.150
father during this process. Of course, this is not a end goal. I'm not there. I'm not

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:04.350
done. This is a work in progress that I think will go on for a long time. I'm starting

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:12.630
to share some of the findings with my family now and letting them into this. They know

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:18.350
that there's a recording going on, so there is a consent level there. I don't

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:22.670
tell them every single time I turn it on, but they know that I'm, I mean,

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.570
I told them I'm going to do this all the time.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:29.630
So whether or not they forget about it sometimes is certainly part of the

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.290
thing. And that's also something that I, you know,

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.250
struggle with and I have to remind them every once in a while.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.770
So it's sort of fresh in mind.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:43.810
Some interesting findings that I had during this process also was I would

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:51.810
I would submit the transcripts and then I would go back and read the analysis and I would find

00:04:51.810 --> 00:05:07.090
that often or not never the machine would miss attribute a line to someone else which as you

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:17.170
can imagine drastically changes the analysis not only did it miss a tribute but it would also miss

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:27.090
here and both of those would result in completely wrong analysis which i would then have to go back

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.850
and correct and the reason why i could go back and correct is because i was the one that was

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:37.090
there I was in the conversation and I luckily would do it the night of so I didn't have enough

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:44.210
time for these things to disappear from me right and that process led me down another

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:55.490
realization which was that recorders are not always right and people aren't always checking

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:06.050
their work and that's a very dangerous thing because a fact can be planted which is not

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:10.770
actually a fact at all which is a complete fabricated piece of information and if someone's

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:15.890
not going back and checking that then you know down the line there are compounding effects

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:23.410
downstream that how do you ever go back and and find that where is the the wrong you know

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:36.410
So that opened up another line of my work, which is tracking AI and making sure that it doesn't say it knows something if it doesn't know something.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:42.410
And it is tedious and I write about it in my other works and you'll certainly see more about that.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:46.410
But yeah, this process also helped me see that.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:52.330
helped me see that. So not only is it helping me as a father and a man, but it's also helping

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:57.750
me with my work with AI. And hopefully my work with AI will help other people and help

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:06.490
AI in general. Like, look, maybe who knows? But that's the idea. You know, another

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:14.630
Another thing about this, you know, I got sober, I stopped drinking a couple years

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:19.590
ago and the reason why was because I wanted to be a better dad, right?

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:27.010
And so this practice is just like the next stage in that and I think that when we as

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:32.470
individuals become aware of some of our failings, we have a responsibility to do

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:38.110
something about it. Otherwise, it's just performative, right? We just talk about it because it makes

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:43.890
us sound better. But if we don't actually change, then it doesn't do anything. What

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:48.590
part of the findings that I was talking about there earlier was, you know, how

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:51.510
it would misattribute things. But one of the other interesting findings was that

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:59.450
when it wasn't sure, it would tend to give me the benefit of the doubt or not

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:07.930
necessarily getting me the benefit of the doubt, but it would tend to flatter me if it was an ambiguous thing because I was the master or the subject or whatever.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:21.330
And that is exactly the opposite of what I wanted to do, which goes back to more lessons I have about the AI, which is just because you prompt it, just because you set up guardrails, just because you set up rules and, you know, ideas that need to be followed.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:29.130
They don't last forever, so there is a upkeep, a maintenance that you as a user are responsible

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.450
for.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.530
Just to go back a little bit to the whole consent piece, because I think this is an

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:38.590
important piece of this all, they're kids.

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:40.010
They can't really consent.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:45.430
They know what's happening, but they can't really consent because they're minors.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:53.400
So that's something that I'm working on, and we talk about it, but a rule that I have in

00:08:53.400 --> 00:09:01.840
place for this is that my failings are the thing to talk about.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:02.840
Not theirs.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:04.400
Not their interpersonal life.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.160
Not the struggles that they're going through.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:11.240
Not even their successes, because that's their life, and that's private for them.

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:16.480
But my reaction to those things is fair game, and that's the distinction that I hold,

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:24.860
I hope that that is enough. I know that this will evolve. I know that some people might

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:31.500
have questions about where does this content live, where do the recordings live, and

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:35.740
that is a very valid question and it is also something that I am constantly working

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:41.580
on and constantly researching. I will say that the device that I use is a Plod. That's

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:48.730
That's not to say that there can't be some breaches down the line.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.530
It's a risk reward that I'm taking right now.

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:55.950
But yeah, I know that some people might have something to say about that.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.410
So I want to, you know, come clean on it because that's my whole thing.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.090
I'd rather no recorder needed.

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:12.250
One moment from this week where you're not sure if you got it right with your

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:17.770
kid, right? Leave the names out. Don't give private personal

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:21.790
details, no need for all that. And then ask your AI of choice.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:26.690
What did I miss? Give it the context, give it the

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:32.170
background. And then just ask the question, what did I miss?

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:37.730
And see, does it give you the truth? Does it flatter

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:42.010
you? Does it make something up that because it doesn't have

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:48.010
of context, these are the questions and these are the experiments that I welcome you to have. So

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:58.330
yeah, there's a lot here. I'm looking forward to reading your comments, I'm looking forward to

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:03.850
engaging with you, probably debating with some of you about this, probably protecting myself

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:13.610
from some anger from the mob but uh I've committed to doing this in public and so it comes with the

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:22.490
course so cross your arms at this doubt me doubt the machine doubt all of it I mean it's better

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:30.730
that way please do you know but check check that's what you can do I wanted you to see a

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:36.170
human here. I wanted you to hear it from me first. The, uh, the words are coming next,

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:40.330
so you'll be able to dig into it a little bit more. But like I said,

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:49.850
this is me. This is what I'm doing and why. And, uh, I talk about this with some of my

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:58.140
clients and I think that some people are really interested in this and I think that it

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:06.250
is a very useful and powerful tool. So take of it what you will. Gauge out.
